---
import { sitePath } from '../data/site';
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import { release } from '../data/site';
---
<Guide title="When a replay stops" description="Start with the first missing requirement or diverging response. Keep the report alongside the capture so the next attempt has a clear hypothesis." sections={[{id:'diagnose',label:'Inspect the run'},{id:'common',label:'Common issues'},{id:'support',label:'Share a safe report'}]}>
  <h2 id="diagnose">Inspect before changing the test</h2><Code code={"livewire version\nlivewire check issue.pcap -details\nlivewire help troubleshoot"} label="Collect the version and capture assessment" /><p>Confirm that your command matches the installed version, your target is reachable, and the selected session contains the requests and responses you expect.</p>
  <h2 id="common">Common stopping points</h2>
  <details class="faq" open><summary>The TLS capture needs a key log</summary><div><p>Supply the NSS key log recorded by the original endpoint, not a key log from a later connection. Ciphertext alone cannot recover the application requests. Keep the file local and pass it explicitly with <code>-keylog</code>.</p><p><a href={sitePath("/secure-replay/")}>Follow the secure replay workflow →</a></p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>The target certificate cannot be verified</summary><div><p>Check the target hostname, expected server name, certificate dates, and local/device clock. Provide a private CA with <code>-ca</code> and use <code>-server-name</code> when connecting by IP. Keep certificate verification enabled.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>The capture has gaps or missing responses</summary><div><p>Inspect the original recording for missing directions, truncated frames, and incomplete streams. An incomplete recording may not supply enough material for request recovery or response comparison. Collect a complete exchange where possible.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>Unknown TCP or an unsupported protocol is blocked</summary><div><p>A TCP connection is not itself an application specification. Check the detected protocol and the supported adapter limits. Choose stateless replay only if you intend to send recorded frames without reconstructing or verifying the session.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>The packet interface cannot open</summary><div><p>List interfaces with <code>livewire ifaces</code> and use the exact interface name. On Windows, packet routes need Npcap and Administrator rights. On Linux, use the documented raw-network capabilities or elevated execution. Socket-based application sessions do not need those packet privileges.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>The target behaves differently</summary><div><p>Read the first differing transaction and check target state, timing, authentication, and dynamic fields. Use supported scenario bindings for live values; do not disable comparison merely to obtain a successful exit. Repeat a bounded number of attempts to distinguish consistent from intermittent differences.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>Packet replay sent everything but the server did not respond</summary><div><p>A successful frame send confirms transmission only. Captured addresses, TCP sequence numbers, and TLS records belong to the original environment. For fresh session behavior, use <code>live</code> with supported application requests.</p></div></details>
  <details class="faq"><summary>A resumed run refuses an uncertain operation</summary><div><p>Resume skips confirmed completed boundaries; it cannot prove whether an interrupted state-changing request took effect. Inspect target state and the journal before choosing a new run. Fresh credentials and connections are required.</p></div></details>
  <h2 id="support">Share a report without the secrets</h2><Code code={"livewire bundle -report issue.report.json -evidence issue.actual.pcap -o issue.support.zip"} label="Create a metadata support bundle" /><p>The bundle references packet evidence by digest rather than embedding the capture. Review all shared metadata. Do not attach TLS key logs, private keys, passwords, or production captures to a public issue.</p><p><a href={`${release.repository}/issues`}>Open a GitHub issue ↗</a> with the version, platform, selected workflow, expected result, and redacted report. Include a synthetic reproducer when possible.</p><p class="reference-link"><a href={sitePath("/reference/operations/")}>Operations and recovery reference →</a></p>
</Guide>
